  "result": "I stopped without reaching OK because the node itself is wrong. The files are left as the record states them, so the gate's verdict on them is **UNANCHORED_VARIABLE**.\n\nI used 4 of the 6 gate runs. Two were wasted by mistake: I ran the gate twice on the untouched skeleton, once inside an exploratory shell command.\n\n**The node's defects** (written up in `task_result.md`):\n1. **The left-turn exception (s5) can't be tied to the subject.** It is read at \"some intersection or driveway/alley entrance\", and the only link to the subject is the declared intention. The gate doesn't accept that as a tie. Adding one myself, such as \"on the highway of the roadway the subject occupies\", would narrow an exception, which isn't allowed. The plan has to state the tie and claim the atoms or parameters it needs.\n2. **branch_1–4 are planned as `compliant`, but each describes an exception that holds.** The record says the duty applies only when no exception holds, so these come out `not_applicable`. Either their verdicts change, or the exceptions move into the obligation and the record says so.\n3. **branch_5 can never be `violated`.** The electric-scooter aggregate (`DEF-NRS-484B-018`) includes no road-user class and lists `ru.electric_scooter` as unresolved. A scooter subject's class is therefore always unknown, and the gate returned `unknown` (aggregate unresolved).\n\n**Diagnostic run:** I added that tie temporarily for one run, then removed it. With it in place:\n- **Passed:** forbid (violated), permit (compliant), idle (not applicable), blind (unknown, only from the masked outlines), and two witnesses I added. Those cover the driveway half of the left-turn exception and debris ahead on the right.\n- **Failed:** only branch_1–5, for exactly the reasons above.\n\n**Choices the node left open:**\n- The gap to the right edge is written doubled (−2·offset − width ≤ 2·gap), because no literal 2 may enter the rule.\n- Core's bearing measure takes components `\"x\"` (along) and `\"y\"` (across), so those are used.\n- \"From zero to the reach\" for an obstruction ahead includes both ends.\n- No narrowings were declared.\n\nFiles are in the library:\n- `TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_777_1_o1.lean`\n- `TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_777_1_o1.lean`\n\nThe report is in the working directory:\n- `task_result.md`",
